roofline control variant `fused_c1` of workloads/clusterfusion_deepseek_v2_lite_mla.yaml (applied by the runner in the
worktree roofline/build/src/ClusterFusion__clusterfusion__deepseek_cluster_size_1/, never in third_party/).
Upstream's CLUSTER_SIZE 1 build of the DeepSeek MLA kernel is wrong, not only untested (found in R7 by reading
include/H100/deepseek/kernel.cuh; three stages hard-code the cluster-4 work split):
0. config.h: CLUSTER_SIZE 4 -> 1 (one CTA per head, 16 CTAs; the cluster reduce / gather loops run zero rounds, which
   is correct for N = 1: dsm.cuh runs N-2 shift rounds for the reduces and N-1 for the QUK all-gather).
1. RMSNorm prologue (kernel.cuh l.119-125): the normalisation loop reuses x from the registers of the last iteration
   of the sum loop; correct only for DIM_PER_BLOCK = HIDDEN_DIM / CLUSTER_SIZE = BLOCK_SIZE * 4 = 512 (cluster 4).
   With 2048 (cluster 1) every chunk would be normalised from chunk 3. Fix: reload the chunk from `input` (read-only).
   Same bug pattern as the Llama kernel (patches/clusterfusion__cluster_size_1.patch).
2. q_nope @ W_uk (l.352-388): CTA b computes the 128 latent outputs [b*128, b*128+128) of the 512 and the QUK
   all-gather collects the four slices. With one CTA only q_lat[0..128) was computed; q_lat[128..512) kept the
   uninitialised bytes of local_qkv. Fix: loop over KV_LORA_RANK / 128 / CLUSTER_SIZE slices of 128 (TMA column
   offset + s * 128), results kept in registers and written after the last slice (the first slice's output overwrites
   q_nope = local_qkv[0..128), which every slice reads), block.sync at the end of each slice before the next TMA reuses
   weight[].
3. a_lat @ W_uv (l.601-637): CTA b contracts rows [b*128, b*128+128) of W_uv (loop bound `128 / TMA_LOAD_ONCE`, tail
   offset `NOPE_HEAD_DIM - TMA_LOAD_ONCE` = 64 = 128 - 64). With one CTA only a_lat[0..128) entered the head output.
   Fix: bounds KV_LORA_RANK / CLUSTER_SIZE (= 128 for cluster 4, numerically unchanged there).
4. TMA-buffer WAR (same pattern as the Llama kernel, where it was the cause of the cluster-4 failures, see
   patches/clusterfusion__residual_out_c4_fix.patch fix 2): the W_q, W_q_pe, W_kv (+ its per-slice restart), W_k_pe,
   flash-decoding and W_uv loops refill TMA buffer id % 2 while warps 1-3 may still read the previous tile from it;
   block.sync() at the top of each. Not observed in the DeepSeek kernel (fused_c1 passed 20/20 before); added so that
   both fused builds run the same code (the cluster-4 patch carries the same lines). Same for the block.sync() before
   the W_UV partial is written into local_qkv[0..128) (with one CTA that range holds a_lat rows the other warps read;
   at most one tile of lag makes it unreachable here, it is a real race in CTA 0 of the cluster-4 build).
For CLUSTER_SIZE 4 fixes 1 and 3 are numerically no-ops and fix 2 differs only by one extra block.sync; fused_c4 is
built with patches/clusterfusion__residual_out_c4_fix.patch (fix 4 and the dsm.cuh hardening, no fixes 1-3). Not changed (unobservable in the output, identical in both fused builds): the k_pe RoPE
partner index (l.305 misses `+ KV_LORA_RANK`) and the q_pe / k_pe values, which the attention never reads.
